<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hobyo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hobyo is a port town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> coast of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>, in the Mudug region. It was the capital of the Sultanate of Hobyo, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ali-kenadid">Yusuf Ali Kenadid</a> around 1878, which exported livestock, hides and gum until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> annexed it in 1925. In the 2000s the town became known as a base for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> piracy.</p></div>
